WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.550
The European Union is the Windows of politics.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:16.059
It´s slow, it doesn't work perfectly OK and
sometimes it gets “crashes”.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:21.580
Nonetheless, let's be honest, the other alternatives
are not much better… and can certainly be

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.580
more costly.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:29.520
At the beginning of this year, it seemed like
the far right was unstoppable.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.980
Some political analysts claimed that Brexit
would be the beginning of the end of European

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:34.980
Union.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.390
And during this time the international media
was full of words like FREXIT or CZEXIT.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.290
However, this Euroskeptic furor wasn't to
last long.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.860
France has elected a brand new president,
Emmanuel Macron, who stands up for the European

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.990
Union like no one else.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.340
The same happened in other elections around
Europe.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.340
In other words…

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.710
the European Union is alive and kicking.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.020
At least, for the next four years.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:03.350
But hold on a minute because things are more
complex than what they seem to be...

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:07.850
In fact, not all EU fans are the same, many
of them don’t even share the same opinion

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.670
on what the EU should be.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:16.680
For instance, Macron stands for a fiscal union,
with the same taxes in every country.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:22.020
But Angela Merkel, nor Jean Claude Juncker
are into that.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.960
On the other hand, the former Belgium Prime
Minister, Guy (Gee) Verhofstadt, who now is

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.369
the President of the European Liberal party,
says that Europe should become a FEDERATION,

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:32.909
like the United States.

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:35.369
But… does everyone agree with that?

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:37.709
Well, the answer is, rather unsurprisingly,
no.

00:01:37.709 --> 00:01:44.170
In fact, the only thing shared by all these
politicians is the fact that EU is a good

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.549
thing.

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:46.929
But…

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:50.509
well, what is the European Union all about?

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:51.579
What should it become?

00:01:51.579 --> 00:01:53.869
Is it a federation… or a confederation?

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:56.680
And what are the different models on the negotiation
table?

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:02.569
Well, today, we are going to answer these
questions!

00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:10.250
WHAT IF MARGARET THATCHER WAS RIGHT?

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.420
Margaret Thatcher is something like Elvis
Presley to Eurosceptics.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.490
For decades, this woman, who was the British
Prime Minister in the 1980s, has become the

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:22.690
biggest inspiration for many of the movements
that want to end the European project.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:28.290
But then again, reality is seldom simple.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:33.060
Now, it is true that Margaret Thatcher was
a big critic of political integration.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.450
Back in the time, the European Union still
didn’t exist.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.010
It was just a community of countries that
traded among themselves.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.600
Nevertheless, during the 1980s, the different
European governments agreed to deepen this

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.780
integration.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:51.170
This is when they started talking about a
single currency and new institutions.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.280
All of this culminatedn 1992, with the signing
of the Maastrich Treaty.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.280
But…

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.320
what did Margaret Thatcher think about all
of this?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.790
The truth is, if we forget about stereotypes
and we, actually, read her memoir, we find

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.260
quotes like this one:

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:12.120
“Britain does not dream of some cosy, isolated
existents on the fringes of the European Community.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:17.100
Our destiny is in Europe, as part of the Community”
--Margaret Thatcher, “The Downing Street

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.100
Years”

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.160
But, importantly, this doesn't mean Thatcher
was in total agreement with all the European

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.370
politicians - she just wanted a different
model.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.380
Unlike those who wanted a United States of
Europe, with the capital in Brussels, she

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.120
stood for a confederate model.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:37.280
“Certainly, we want to see Europe more united
and with a greater sense of common purpose.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:42.030
But it must be in a way which preserves the
different traditions, parliamentary powers

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.720
and sense of national pride in one's own country”
--Margaret Thatcher, “The Downing Street

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.720
Years”

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.880
But before we keep going, we really must explain:
What is the difference between a FEDERATION

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.370
and a CONFEDERATION?

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:59.620
An example of a federation would be the United
States of America.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:04.290
Texas and California have their own parliaments,
their own governments, and their own laws.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.920
Today, for instance, marijuana is legal in
California but it is forbidden in Texas.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:15.980
However, if Congress (in Washington DC) passed
a law legalizing cannabis, any state law that

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.160
contradicted the federal law one would be
automatically abolished.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.959
In a confederation, states have way more autonomy.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:25.370
Today, there are actually no confederations
in the world.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:26.630
Not even Switzerland.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:30.680
Of course, in Switzerland, the different cantons
enjoy a lot of autonomy and even different

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.680
taxes…

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.480
But that doesn’t mean they are a confederation!

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.880
For instance, if the Parliament at Berna would
pass a law legalizing marijuana, the rest

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:44.540
of the cantons would have to accept it.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:48.590
It Switzerland was a real confederation, each
of the different assemblies would have to

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:52.540
have a vote to decide if they want to keep
cannabis legal or not.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.500
So, despite what a lot of people say, Switzerland
is clearly a federation.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.620
And now you might be wondering, well, what
is Europe?

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.710
Is it a federation or a confederation?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.850
Of course, there are a lot of people who stand
for the federal model.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:16.400
In the last few years, the champion of this
idea has been the President of the Liberals,

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:25.210
Guy (Gee)Verhofstadt.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.730
But let’s go back to the facts.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:31.020
Today, despite what it looks, national governments
have a lot of autonomy.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:35.330
For instance, years ago, Brussels passed a
directive banning smoking in bars.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.770
After that, each of the member countries had
to vote on their own anti-tobacco law.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.430
And do you know what happened?

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.430
Well…

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.030
Austria and Czech Republic did not pass those
laws.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:49.400
And during those years, you could smoke in
the cafes of Prague or Vienna while in Berlin

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:54.690
and Paris it was completely forbidden.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:06:02.150
Even the VAT, which is the main European tax,
is different in each country.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:08.080
In Spain, they pay a 21%, but in Hungary they
pay 27%, and in Germany, they’ve got a 19%.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.240
tax In other words, Europe is not a federation.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.900
But is not a confederation, either.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.710
It´s kind of a… “federal confederation.”

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:16.710
And now you might wonder…

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.639
Is this federal confederation model actually
working?

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:24.500
Or do we need to move ahead with some sort
of “United States of Europe”?

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.680
WHAT´S WRONG IN EUROPEAN UNION?

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.190
We've all have heard about the many mistakes
this European integration has made.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:36.240
But the truth is many of these flaws could
have happened in all the member states individually.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.490
As an example let us consider the refugee
crisis.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:43.150
Now, it is true that Brussels was incapable
of crafting a common policy to give asylum

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:47.639
to all the citizens that are running away
from countries like Syria, Iraq or Libya.

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:49.240
But let’s not lie to ourselves!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.290
The same happened in every single country.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:57.430
In Spain, the national government of did everything
they could to avoid welcoming the refugees.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:02.030
On the other hand, Madrid’s city hall did
the exact opposite.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:08.330
“The City Hall of Madrid will make a welcoming
project, so the refugees will have a place

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.330
to live”

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:13.320
In other words, we cannot expect Brussels
to solve the problems that nation-states have

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.360
always had.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:17.199
In politics, such things are simple not possible.

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:21.690
But hold on a moment because this doesn't
mean European Union is perfect either.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:26.480
In fact, there are many problems that are
endemic to this institution.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:32.550
For example, imagine you are a freelancer
living in Hungary and you work for a company

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.979
based in Belgium.

00:07:33.979 --> 00:07:36.010
Should you include the VAT on that invoice?

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:41.210
According to the EU legislation, you shouldn't
because it is a service contract.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:46.169
But each country has it's own tax laws that,
in many cases, contradict the EU laws.

00:07:46.169 --> 00:07:47.640
But not only that!

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.100
What VAT should you include on the invoice?

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.139
The Hungarian or the Belgium one?

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:57.050
All this problems could be solved if there
was a common ground on taxation matters.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:08:00.820
But many countries don't want to lose sovereignty
on this matter.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:04.050
And no one dares make the first step towards
this...

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:11.300
So, as you might imagine, it’s hard for
important decisions to move forward…

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:17.710
So, what could be the solution to this problem?

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:21.400
A CLUB WITH DIFFERENT KINDS OF MEMBERS?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.400
Constitutions are useful.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.410
They allow politicians and legislators to
know what they can do and what they cannot.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:30.229
It is like a minimal agreement.

00:08:30.229 --> 00:08:34.111
This way, a government knows what that it
can pass as a law, it’s a system that time

00:08:34.111 --> 00:08:36.329
has proven effective.

00:08:36.329 --> 00:08:39.599
So, what’s the problem?

00:08:39.599 --> 00:08:43.240
Well, all attempts to release a European Constitution
have failed.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:49.370
In 2005, both France and Netherlands had referendums
where they rejected the proposal for a European

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.690
Magna Carta.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:54.450
Years later, Brussels politicians met again
to write a new version of this constitution,

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.310
the so-called Lisbon Treaty.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:09:00.110
This was a milder version of the previously
drafted constitution.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.480
But integration problems persisted…

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.380
The truth is that each country has its own
interests and it’s hard to get them all

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.420
on the same page.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:10.380
So… why not recognize the differences?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:15.290
And this is why, the European Commission has
made the European White Book where they imagine

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:21.020
five potential scenarios for EU reform.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:24.790
One of them would allow each state to have
a different level of integration.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:29.740
On the other hand, at the beginning of 2017,
The Economist proposed to create a European

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:32.090
Union with different kinds of membership.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.620
On one hand, there would be the “Premium
members,” those who share a common currency,

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:39.210
common fiscal policy, and common foreign policy.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:42.500
On the other hand, there will be the “Silver
members,” who just share a common market

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.990
and free movement.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:47.740
Other members, let´s call them “Bronze
members”, will have access to just the common

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:49.570
market.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:54.300
This way, it would be way easier to convince
every country to pass a common European Constitution.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:58.740
Meanwhile, the idea of a United States of
Europe has lost a lot of supporters.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:04.450
The idea of a Europe with different membership
levels currently enjoys a lot more support.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:09.560
Meanwhile, France’s brand new president
is willing to play a major role on the future

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:10.560
of Europe.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.300
But what does he really stand for?

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:18.900
Well, if you want to know more about Emmanuel
Macron, don´t forget to check out this video.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:22.790
And now the question is…

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:27.800
Do you think this hybrid of a federal confederation,
with different member categories, can actually

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:28.800
work?

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:32.180
Or we should keep trying for a federation
where everyone has the same rules?

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:34.570
Please, let us know what you think in the
comments section below.

